# Strangers: what they passed on the way here (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Hubs"), one small thing, in their
# own words. Their ask stays theirs, as built.

conv stranger.any.passed
for stranger
topic "What did you pass on the way here?"
prio flavour
once
voice plain

bind horde = news:horde
bind fire = news:burned
bind dead = news:death

node start
  jump news:horde -> horde
  jump news:burned -> fire
  jump news:death -> dead
  say? rain :: "Puddles. I counted them to stop counting other things. Forty-one. Forty-two, if you count the one in my left boot, and I've stopped being able to ignore it."
  say? night :: "Nothing. It's dark. I passed the dark, and a lot of noises I decided weren't anything. I'm very good at deciding that now."
  say "A dog that followed me for a mile and then thought better of it. Somebody's dog, with a collar on. That was the best part of the whole day."
  > @back0 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

node horde
  say "A lot of the sick, near {bind:horde}. All walking the same way, like a parade nobody wanted. I lay in a ditch till the last of them had gone."
  say "The ditch was nice, actually. Quiet. Nobody asked me for anything in the ditch. I might go back to the ditch."
  > @back1 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

node fire
  say "Smoke over {bind:fire}. A whole street of it. I didn't go closer. I'm not that sort of brave. I'm the walking-away sort, and it's kept me alive this long."
  > @back2 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

node dead
  say "Somebody had died near {bind:dead}, by the road. Somebody else had covered them with a coat. A good coat, too, a warm one, in this weather. That stayed with me."
  > @back3 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub
